  "query_preview": "..(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 407 PM EDT FRI OCT 2 2026\n\nRain chances will extend into the start of this period. Higher \nrainfall totals will likely occur across our southeast, closer to \nwhere the better PWATs (1.6-1.8 inches per the latest LREF). There \nis still quite a bit of spread in the guidance, with the 25th-75th \npercentile differing by as much as an inch across our southeast. The \ncurrent forecast has totals on Sunday in the 0.5-0.75 inch range.  \n\nMonday will see the return to calm and quiet conditions across the \nregion. Rain will have cleared out from the previous day and high \npressure will build across the Great Lakes, before migrating further \neast with time. A secondary high pressure system will then build in \nacross the Ohio Valley, sustaining our dry weather through Friday \nwith plenty of opportunities for sunshine. Highs each day through \nthe week should be in the 70s until a few 80s could return in our \nsouthwest as early as Thursday. Lows, especially on Monday and \nTuesday nights, do look to be pretty chilly in the lower 40s. A few \nsheltered valleys could dip into the upper 30s, although model \nguidance does not really support frost quite yet, with fog a better \npossibility in the river valleys.",
